🔴 3. Insecure Storage of Encrypted Credentials with Co-located Key Material
Risk

Critical

CVSS 3.1

9.1 (Critical)

Vulnerability Category

Broken Cryptography / Sensitive Data Exposure

Description

It was observed that encrypted credential files are stored along with their corresponding key and IV files in the same directory. All components required for decryption are accessible from shared network paths. This design defeats the purpose of encryption and allows attackers to recover plaintext credentials. No secure key management mechanism is implemented.

Impact
Full credential disclosure
Unauthorized database access
Complete system compromise
Recommendations

It is recommended to implement secure key management by storing encryption keys separately in a secure vault and restricting access to credential files.

References
https://owasp.org/Top10/A02_2021-Cryptographic_Failures/
PoC Steps

Step 1: Locate .enc, key, and IV files
Step 2: Verify all are in same directory
Step 3: Confirm accessibility
Step 4: Identify decryption feasibility

OWASP Category

A02: Cryptographic Failures

