🔴 7. Insecure LDAP Communication (Non-LDAPS)
Risk

High

CVSS 3.1

8.2 (High)

Vulnerability Category

Insecure Communication

Description

It was observed that LDAP communication is configured without secure protocols such as LDAPS. Communication occurs over standard LDAP, which transmits data in plaintext. Credentials are exposed during transmission over the network. This makes the system vulnerable to interception attacks.

Impact
Credential interception
Man-in-the-middle attacks
Unauthorized access
Recommendations

It is recommended to implement LDAPS over port 636 and enforce TLS encryption for all directory communications.

